{"id": "EUVD-2026-76646", "enisaUuid": "a8c9bde6-768d-331a-964e-6c4beae8f546", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: uvc: Fix null pointer dereference in uvcg_video_init()\n\nIn uvcg_video_init(), if kthread_run_worker() fails,\nthe error logged uses uvcg_err(), however, the pointer it uses:\nvideo->uvc is not assigned at this point, triggering a null\npointer dereference. Fix this by directly using uvc->func which\nis assigned already.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbe2762ae8e543b06c57f1ac6512b02fd3fd09b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d511e015d06767f52bb18d48371cab6d7cb88433", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b1da38592efdc1a263d4c0353298cba19e9d6fc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v583-q5v7-76fp", "CVE-2026-89734"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06d6aeb5-08b7-3016-8cec-97bc91d373cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "1890d7c4-2ee5-36fd-bd85-72ee7fec9961", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "5003a43c-390d-3dea-b111-617677069d83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0bbfbd16b3b67106535299d6a9ca3a5565494a6 <dbe2762ae8e543b06c57f1ac6512b02fd3fd09b2"}, {"id": "5683582c-7f1f-37fa-bb22-48b9ec623372", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0bbfbd16b3b67106535299d6a9ca3a5565494a6 <5b1da38592efdc1a263d4c0353298cba19e9d6fc"}, {"id": "5c7e75f6-3ad5-3ce4-95f8-d70ed9cb3284", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "5fc9018c-c4d8-3821-b979-3e0b959c65ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0bbfbd16b3b67106535299d6a9ca3a5565494a6 <d511e015d06767f52bb18d48371cab6d7cb